{title: Joyful, Joyful, We Adore Thee}
{artist: Henry van Dyke (1852-1933)}
{key: G}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[G]Joyful, joyful, [D]we adore Thee, [G]God of glory, [D]Lord of love;
[G]Hearts unfold like [D]flowers be[Em]fore Thee, [C]opening to the [D]sun a[G]bove.
[D]Melt the clouds of [G]sin and sadness, [D]drive the dark of [G]doubt away;
[Em]Giver of im[Bm]mortal gladness, [C]fill us with the [D]light of [G]day.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[G]All Thy works with [D]joy surround Thee, [G]earth and heaven re[D]flect Thy rays,
[G]Stars and angels [D]sing a[Em]round Thee, [C]center of un[D]broken [G]praise.
[D]Field and forest, [G]vale and mountain, [D]flowery meadow, [G]flashing sea,
[Em]Chanting bird and [Bm]flowing fountain [C]call us to re[D]joice in [G]Thee.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[G]Thou art giving [D]and forgiving, [G]ever blessing, [D]ever blest,
[G]Wellspring of the [D]joy of [Em]living, [C]ocean depth of [D]happy [G]rest!
[D]Thou our Father, [G]Christ our Brother, [D]all who live in [G]love are Thine;
[Em]Teach us how to [Bm]love each other, [C]lift us to the [D]joy di[G]vine.
{eov}
